    <!-- FAQ -->
    <string name="faq_general">GENERAL QUESTIONS</string>
    <string name="faq_q1">What is Speye?</string>
    <string name="faq_a1">Speye is a free app to keep track of your notifications and never lose them.</string>
    <string name="faq_q2">How can I backup my notifications?</string>
    <string name="faq_a2">You can export your notifications to a .spy file in the Settings page and import them back whenever you want, on any device. Alternatively, you can connect your Google Drive account to make periodic backups of your data and restore it.</string>
    <string name="faq_q3">Is Speye free?</string>
    <string name="faq_a3">Speye is completely free and to use and is open source, but contains ads. You can make a 1-time purchase to remove ads forever. Alternatively, you can get the ad-free version from F-Droid, but you\'ll lose the ability to connect to Google Drive.</string>

    <string name="faq_security">SECURITY QUESTIONS</string>
    <string name="faq_q4">Does Speye store my data?</string>
    <string name="faq_a4">Speye does not store any remote data by itself and saves your notifications in your local storage. Google AdMob services may use your account data for targeted ads, which is not controlled by Speye itself.</string>
    <string name="faq_q5">How does cloud sync work?</string>
    <string name="faq_a5">By default, all data stays on your device. If you enable Google Drive Backup, an encrypted .spy file is stored in your private app data folder. A .spy file only contains saved notification data such as texts and attachments.</string>
    <string name="faq_q6">Can others view my texts?</string>
    <string name="faq_a6">Speye doesn\'t and will never share your personal data. However, if someone copies your .spy backup, they can import it on their phone to view your notification history.</string>

    <string name="faq_misc">MISCELLANEOUS QUESTIONS</string>
    <string name="faq_q7">How can I enable debugging mode?</string>
    <string name="faq_a7">In the Settings page, click the Speye logo 5 times.</string>
    <string name="faq_q8">How can I report a bug?</string>
    <string name="faq_a8">From the debugging options, enable the Enable logging option, then proceed with your desired action (import/export, cloud login etc.). In the activity logs, any error should now be visible. Copy them and share them with me through the contact option on the Settings page.</string>
    <string name="faq_q9">How can I test the notifications?</string>
    <string name="faq_a9">From the debugging options, enable the Show Test Button option and return back to the History page. You will now be able to access the test button to send yourself different types of test notifications.</string>

    <!-- Privacy Policy -->
    <string name="privacy_title">PRIVACY POLICY</string>
    <string name="privacy_data_collection">DATA COLLECTION</string>
    <string name="privacy_local_storage">Local Storage</string>
    <string name="privacy_local_storage_text">Speye is designed with privacy in mind. All notification data, including text, history, and image attachments, is stored locally on your device in a private database. We do not store or transmit any sensitive data by ourselves.</string>
    <string name="privacy_third_party">Third-Party Services</string>
    <string name="privacy_third_party_text">While Speye itself does not store or transmit any sensitive data, the Google Play version of the app integrates third-party services like AdMob and Google Play Services. These services may collect certain information, such as device identifiers and usage statistics, which could be used for ad personalization and analytics. We recommend reviewing Google\'s Privacy Policy for more details.</string>
    <string name="privacy_cloud">Cloud Backup</string>
    <string name="privacy_cloud_text">If you choose to enable Google Drive Backup, Speye uploads your data to a private folder in your personal Google Drive account. This data is not accessible by the developers or any other third parties, and stays under your control.</string>

